    {
      "id": "288d3186bc814bc0",
      "role": "C",
      "mission": {
        "base_commit": "cb615a823931a8471527db73839f8ca439ef0f69",
        "delegation_parent": "R/C",
        "depth": 1,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "A single OpenMP team reused across the ten simulation iterations, with static worksharing over independent bodies, can reduce parallel-region startup overhead while retaining useful parallelism for sufficiently large systems. Each body's force accumulation remains serial in the original j order, preserving its arithmetic order.",
        "id": "288d3186bc814bc0",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "C",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/nbody.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Replaced serial outer-body force traversal with an orphaned OpenMP for loop using schedule(static), keeping each body's force accumulators private and in the original accumulation order.",
            "Created one OpenMP parallel region around all iterations and statically workshared the position-update loop, amortizing team startup and retaining the required phase barriers.",
            "Added a body-count threshold for team creation to limit overhead on small inputs."
          ]
        },
        "tree_id": "e1:C",
        "trial_id": "01M5449N47VPZSRV5KRDWEA5Y0",
